+# Fälligkeitsdatum für Todos Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Todos get an optional `dueDate` (`YYYY-MM-DD`), a server-computed `overdue` flag (UTC), a `GET /todos?overdue=true|false` filter, and the list page shows date, a red „überfällig“ marker and a „nur überfällige“ checkbox.
+
+**Architecture:** `src/store.mjs` stores `{ id, title, done, dueDate }`, validates `dueDate`, and returns copies enriched with `overdue` computed by the pure `isOverdue(todo, today)` against an injectable clock. `src/app.mjs` only gains query-param parsing for the filter. `public/index.html` renders the new fields and the filter checkbox.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Node 24, ES modules, `node:http`, `node:test`, no dependencies.
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-11-faelligkeitsdatum-design.md`
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- Zero dependencies — Node builtins only.
+- Validation errors are `ValidationError` from `src/store.mjs` ⇒ HTTP 400 (already mapped in `app.mjs`).
+- TDD: failing test in `test/` first. Run all tests with `npm test`.
+- Every todo in every response has exactly `{ id, title, done, dueDate, overdue }`.
+- dueDate error message: `dueDate must be a date in YYYY-MM-DD format or null`.
+- Filter error message: `overdue must be true or false`.
+- „Today“ is the UTC date: `now().toISOString().slice(0, 10)`.
+- New UI elements carry `data-testid`: `todo-due-date`, `todo-overdue`, `filter-overdue`.
+- UI copy: `überfällig`, `nur überfällige`.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+- PATCH with a valid field plus an invalid one (`{ done: true, dueDate: "x" }`) ⇒ 400 and **no** partial update (today `update` mutates before validating later fields) — test in Task 1.
+- POST with valid title and invalid `dueDate` ⇒ 400 and nothing stored (no todo in `list()`) — test in Task 1.
+- Leap days: `2028-02-29` valid, `2027-02-29` invalid; empty string `""` invalid — test in Task 1.
+- `?overdue=TRUE` / `?overdue=1` ⇒ 400 (exact `true`/`false` only) — test in Task 2.
+- Fast filter toggling: a slow earlier response must not overwrite the list for the current checkbox state — handled in Task 3 (render only if checkbox state still matches the request), verified in E2E.
+
+---
+
